{"type":"assistant","message":{"id":"064b75400ace0710e85303ab993a16d8","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"The user is asking about macOS Terminal.app .terminal plist file format. They want:\n1. What key fields a .terminal plist should have (name, ProfileCurrentVersion, Font, ANSIColors)\n2. Where imported .terminal files appear in Terminal.app\n3. Whether `defaults write com.apple.Terminal Default Window Settings` is needed to set default\n4. Mechanical verification command snippets\n\nLet me think about what I know about macOS Terminal .terminal plist files:\n\n1. **Key fields in a .terminal plist**:\n   - `name` - the profile name\n   - `ProfileCurrentVersion` - version number (typically 1.0 or something like that)\n   - `Font` - usually has `AFRF` (family name) and size\n   - `ANSIColors` - dictionary with color values for ANSI colors (AnsiBlack, AnsiRed, AnsiGreen, AnsiYellow, AnsiBlue, AnsiMagenta, AnsiCyan, AnsiWhite)\n   - Also typically `TextBoldColor`, `TextColor`, `BackgroundColor`, `CursorColor`, etc.\n   - `KeyboardHotkey` might also be present\n\n2. **Where imported .terminal files appear**:\n   - They get added to Terminal's preferences\n   - Actually, when you double-click or `open` a .terminal file, it imports the profile into Terminal.app's settings\n   - The profiles are stored in `~/Library/Preferences/com.apple.Terminal.plist`\n   - Or more specifically in `~/Library/Containers/com.apple.Terminal/Data/Library/Preferences/com.apple.Terminal.plist`\n\n3. **Setting default**:\n   - `defaults write com.apple.Terminal Default Window Settings -string \"ProfileName\"` sets the default window setting\n   - `defaults write com.apple.Terminal NSGlobalDomain NSFont` is different and not the right approach\n   - The correct key is `Default Window Settings` or `Window Settings`\n\nFor mechanical verification, I should provide commands to:\n1. Read a .terminal plist file to verify its contents\n2. Check where Terminal stores profiles\n3. Verify the default window setting has been applied\n\nLet me write this in Chinese as requested.","signature":"d8cdd0b6b12f2c8231a77b9814816f2aa7a239aa565dfe5dc9458ac1d24cb1c5"}],"model":"MiniMax-M2.7-highspeed","stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":159,"output_tokens":0,"cache_creation_input_tokens":21500,"cache_read_input_tokens":25668},"service_tier":"standard","context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"d886635e-62c1-4dc0-aeb6-be9992ce5ed5","uuid":"96635945-7883-4899-bb30-9577962e031d"}
